<title>MALAYSIA: Rubberex debuts at 7.00 ringgit.</title>
<headline>Rubberex debuts at 7.00 ringgit.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian rubber glove maker Rubberex Corp (M) Bhd debuted on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange on Wednesday at seven ringgit against a 2.25 ringgit offer price.</p>
<p>The stock went as high as 7.20 ringgit. At 0138 GMT, it was trading at 6.70 ringgit.  </p>
<p>Rubberex had offered 4.631 million shares.</p>
<p>For the year ended December 31, 1997, the company has forecast an after-tax profit of 5.18 million ringgit, or 18 cents a share against an after-tax profit of 5.03 million or 27 cents a share earned in 1996.</p>
<p>The company makes general purpose and industrial rubber gloves.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 206 2323)</p>
